ion&#x60;: requires &#x60;leadGenFormId&#x60; (an adForm ID from POST /v1/ads/lead-forms). Sets the campaign objective to MAX_LEAD and the creative&#39;s &#x60;leadgenCallToAction&#x60; destination to &#x60;urn:li:adForm:{id}&#x60;. - &#x60;job_applicants&#x60;: requires a &#x60;platformSpecificData.jobs&#x60; creative. - &#x60;conversions&#x60; or promoting an existing post: use POST /v1/ads/boost.  **OpenAI Ads**  - Only &#x60;traffic&#x60;, &#x60;awareness&#x60;, &#x60;conversions&#x60; (other goals return 400). They map to OpenAI&#39;s &#x60;bidding_type&#x60; (clicks, impressions, conversions). - &#x60;conversions&#x60; needs an active conversion event setting on the account, or returns 400. Create a tracking tag with &#x60;defaultEventType&#x60; (&#x60;POST /v1/accounts/{accountId}/tracking-tags&#x60;) or configure one in OpenAI Ads Manager. - Pick the event with &#x60;promotedObject.customEventType&#x60; (see AdPromotedObject); without it, the most recently created optimizable event is used.  **Reddit Ads**  - Supported: &#x60;traffic&#x60; (CLICKS), &#x60;awareness&#x60; (BRAND_AWARENESS), &#x60;conversions&#x60;, &#x60;video_views&#x60; (VIDEO_VIEWABLE_IMPRESSIONS), &#x60;lead_generation&#x60; (LEAD_GENERATION). Any other goal returns 400. - &#x60;conversions&#x60;: requires &#x60;promotedObject.customEventType&#x60;; the pixel must already have received that event (see AdPromotedObject). - &#x60;lead_generation&#x60;: sends people to &#x60;linkUrl&#x60; and optimizes toward the pixel&#39;s Lead event, which the pixel must already have received. Reddit retired native lead forms on September 30, 2026, so &#x60;leadGenFormId&#x60; returns 400. - &#x60;video_views&#x60;: needs a &#x60;video&#x60; (422 otherwise); &#x60;optimizationGoal&#x60; picks VIDEO_VIEW_6S (default) or VIDEO_VIEW_15S. 
