        /// Validate the request without creating anything. Any other platform, or a Google campaignType other than pmax or demand_gen, returns 501 &#x60;feature_not_available&#x60;.  **Google Performance Max**: validates the complete atomic campaign and asset group, with no resource creation or local persistence. Validation still downloads image URLs and consumes quota.  **Meta**: validates the inline campaign, ad set, creative and ad with execution_options validate_only. Nothing is uploaded or created; validation bypasses Idempotency-Key storage. Success returns 200 with per-node results; a Meta rejection returns an error.  - Supported: a single image or existing video.id (each also with bodies[] / headlines[] Multiple Text Options), all-image placementAssets with per-rule copy and text pools, or existingCreativeId. - Return 400: dynamicCreative, translations, carouselCards, placement videos, new video uploads, creatives[], adSetId, RESERVED buying. - Placement validation uses existing Instagram identities only. Existing campaign or creative nodes are marked skipped. - When Meta cannot dry-run the nested tree, the campaign and creative are validated alone and the adSet and ad nodes return unverified with the reason. This covers code 2, and two errors Meta returns but then creates normally (below). - Code 1 (unknown error) on an OFFSITE_CONVERSIONS ad set nested in a new campaign (some website-conversion ad sets). - Code 100 subcode 2446880 \&quot;WhatsApp number required\&quot; on an ad that does not message on WhatsApp (intermittent). If the creative&#39;s own dry run also asks for a WhatsApp number, the creative is unverified too. Messaging ads still fail on 2446880.  **ChatGPT (OpenAI)**: no platform dry-run. Zernio runs every check it knows (creative lengths, budget, bid strategy, targeting) plus live lookups of the conversion event and target countries, and uploads or creates nothing. OpenAI&#39;s own checks (image fetch, currency-specific minimums, ad review