        /// <summary>
        /// When present, switches to the attach shape: adds one new ad to this existing ad set without creating a new campaign. Mutually exclusive with &#x60;creatives[]&#x60;.  **Inherited from the ad set on Meta:** budget, targeting, goal, schedule and bid strategy. Passing &#x60;bidStrategy&#x60; in attach mode returns 400 (change an ad set&#39;s bid with &#x60;PUT /v1/ads/ad-sets/{adSetId}&#x60;). &#x60;dynamicCreative&#x60; returns 400 in attach mode: omit &#x60;adSetId&#x60; to create a new dynamic ad set instead.  **Creative.** The attached ad takes the full single-creative surface: &#x60;headline&#x60;/&#x60;body&#x60;/&#x60;description&#x60;/&#x60;callToAction&#x60; plus one of:  - &#x60;imageUrl&#x60;/&#x60;video&#x60; - &#x60;placementAssets&#x60; (its own per-placement Feed/Story assets) - &#x60;translations&#x60;/&#x60;defaultLocale&#x60; (its own per-locale asset feed, Meta only)  Pass &#x60;leadGenFormId&#x60; on EVERY ad attached to a lead ad set: the parent must be ON_AD (true for ad sets created via goal &#x60;lead_generation&#x60;), and Meta rejects a formless ad there.  To build N full ads sharing one ad set, create the first ad via the normal shape, then attach the rest one call each.  **Platforms.** Supported on Meta (facebook, instagram), Google Ads, TikTok, LinkedIn and Reddit Ads.  - TikTok: &#x60;adSetId&#x60; is the ad group ID; the new ad inherits the ad group&#39;s bid, budget and targeting. - LinkedIn: &#x60;adSetId&#x60; is the LinkedIn Campaign ID (numeric). We attach a new Creative to that Campaign, so its &#x60;platformSpecificData&#x60; bidding, targeting, budget and schedule are inherited (passing those fields returns 400). - Reddit Ads: &#x60;adSetId&#x60; is the AD GROUP id. Only the post and the ad are created; the ad group keeps its budget, schedule, targeting, bid and optimization. &#x60;goal&#x60; is not required. An ad group of another ad account returns 404. - Reddit Ads, rejected with 400: &#x60;budgetAmount&#x60;, &#x60;budgetType&#x60;, &#x60;startDate&#x60;, &#x60;endDate&#x60;, targeting fields, &#x60;promotedObject&#x60;, &#x60;tracking.pixelId&#x60; and &#x60;optimizationGoal&#x60;.  **Google Ads.** &#x60;adSetId&#x60; is the AD GROUP id (numeric). &#x60;goal&#x60; is not required: the ad group keeps its campaign&#39;s bidding, budget and targeting. &#x60;validateOnly&#x60; is supported.  - &#x60;campaignType&#x60; is read from the ad group&#39;s campaign (Search, Display or Demand Gen) and can be omitted. A contradicting &#x60;campaignType&#x60; returns 400, an ad group Google does not know in that customer returns 404, and any other campaign type returns 422. - A Search ad needs &#x60;headline&#x60; + &#x60;body&#x60; + &#x60;linkUrl&#x60;; a Display ad also needs &#x60;images.landscape&#x60; + &#x60;images.square&#x60; + &#x60;businessName&#x60;. - Google allows 3 responsive search ads per ad group: a fourth returns 422 naming the limit (&#x60;RESPONSIVE_SEARCH_ADS_PER_AD_GROUP&#x60;) and the ad group. - &#x60;budgetAmount&#x60;/&#x60;budgetType&#x60; and bidding fields (&#x60;bidStrategy&#x60;, &#x60;bidAmount&#x60;, &#x60;portfolioBidStrategyId&#x60;) return 400; the ad group already owns them. - With &#x60;campaignType: \&quot;demand_gen\&quot;&#x60; the ad group must belong to a Demand Gen campaign (otherwise 400). &#x60;demandGen&#x60; carries only the ad&#39;s creative, and the new ad is created PAUSED. - Demand Gen ad group settings return 400: geo, languages, &#x60;demandGen.channels&#x60;/&#x60;audience&#x60;/&#x60;audienceId&#x60;/ &#x60;adGroupName&#x60;. 
