        /// <value>When present, switches to the attach shape: adds one new ad to this existing ad set without creating a new campaign. Mutually exclusive with &#x60;creatives[]&#x60;.  **Inherited from the ad set on Meta:** budget, targeting, goal, schedule and bid strategy. Passing &#x60;bidStrategy&#x60; in attach mode returns 400 (change an ad set&#39;s bid with &#x60;PUT /v1/ads/ad-sets/{adSetId}&#x60;). &#x60;dynamicCreative&#x60; returns 400 in attach mode: omit &#x60;adSetId&#x60; to create a new dynamic ad set instead.  **Creative.** The attached ad takes the full single-creative surface: &#x60;headline&#x60;/&#x60;body&#x60;/&#x60;description&#x60;/&#x60;callToAction&#x60; plus one of:  - &#x60;imageUrl&#x60;/&#x60;video&#x60; - &#x60;placementAssets&#x60; (its own per-placement Feed/Story assets) - &#x60;translations&#x60;/&#x60;defaultLocale&#x60; (its own per-locale asset feed, Meta only)  Pass &#x60;leadGenFormId&#x60; on EVERY ad attached to a lead ad set: the parent must be ON_AD (true for ad sets created via goal &#x60;lead_generation&#x60;), and Meta rejects a formless ad there.  To build N full ads sharing one ad set, create the first ad via the normal shape, then attach the rest one call each.  **Platforms.** Supported on Meta (facebook, instagram), Google Ads, TikTok, LinkedIn and Reddit Ads.  - TikTok: &#x60;adSetId&#x60; is the ad group ID; the new ad inherits the ad group&#39;s bid, budget and targeting. - LinkedIn: &#x60;adSetId&#x60; is the LinkedIn Campaign ID (numeric). We attach a new Creative to that Campaign, so its &#x60;platformSpecificData&#x60; bidding, targeting, budget and schedule are inherited (passing those fields returns 400). - Reddit Ads: &#x60;adSetId&#x60; is the AD GROUP id. Only the post and the ad are created; the ad group keeps its budget, schedule, targeting, bid and optimization. &#x60;goal&#x60; is not required. An ad group of another ad account returns 404. - Reddit Ads, rejected with 400: &#x60;budgetAmount&#x60;, &#x60;budgetType&#x60;, &#x60;startDate&#x60;, &#x60;endDate&#x60;, targeting fields, &#x60;promotedObject&#x60;, &#x60;tracking.pixelId&#x60; and &#x60;optimizationGoal&#x60;.  **Google Ads.** &#x60;adSetId&#x60; is the AD GROUP id (numeric). &#x60;goal&#x60; is not required: the ad group keeps its campaign&#39;s bidding, budget and targeting. &#x60;validateOnly&#x60; is supported.  - &#x60;campaignType&#x60; is read from the ad group&#39;s campaign (Search, Display or Demand Gen) and can be omitted. A contradicting &#x60;campaignType&#x60; returns 400, an ad group Google does not know in that customer returns 404, and any other campaign type returns 422. - A Search ad needs &#x60;headline&#x60; + &#x60;body&#x60; + &#x60;linkUrl&#x60;; a Display ad also needs &#x60;images.landscape&#x60; + &#x60;images.square&#x60; + &#x60;businessName&#x60;. - Google allows 3 responsive search ads per ad group: a fourth returns 422 naming the limit (&#x60;RESPONSIVE_SEARCH_ADS_PER_AD_GROUP&#x60;) and the ad group. - &#x60;budgetAmount&#x60;/&#x60;budgetType&#x60; and bidding fields (&#x60;bidStrategy&#x60;, &#x60;bidAmount&#x60;, &#x60;portfolioBidStrategyId&#x60;) return 400; the ad group already owns them. - With &#x60;campaignType: \&quot;demand_gen\&quot;&#x60; the ad group must belong to a Demand Gen campaign (otherwise 400). &#x60;demandGen&#x60; carries only the ad&#39;s creative, and the new ad is created PAUSED. - Demand Gen ad group settings return 400: geo, languages, &#x60;demandGen.channels&#x60;/&#x60;audience&#x60;/&#x60;audienceId&#x60;/ &#x60;adGroupName&#x60;. </value>
        [DataMember(Name = "adSetId", EmitDefaultValue = false)]
        public string AdSetId { get; set; }

        /// <summary>
        /// Create the new objects under this EXISTING campaign instead of creating a new one. Supported on Meta, Google Ads, LinkedIn, TikTok and Reddit Ads. Mutually exclusive with &#x60;adSetId&#x60; and &#x60;creatives[]&#x60;.  - TikTok: creates the ad group and the ad under this campaign. The campaign is neither created nor activated, and its objective must fit &#x60;goal&#x60;. Not with &#x60;smartPlus&#x60;. - Meta: adds the new ad set under this campaign (multi-ad-set audience testing). Its budget matches the campaign&#39;s mode: for a CBO campaign (campaign-level budget) omit &#x60;budgetAmount&#x60;/&#x60;budgetType&#x60;, since the campaign owns the budget; for an ABO campaign pass them (they go on the new ad set). - LinkedIn: creates a new Campaign (and its Creative) under this EXISTING CampaignGroup. - Google Ads: creates a new ad group under this campaign. It inherits the campaign&#39;s budget, so omit &#x60;budgetAmount&#x60;/&#x60;budgetType&#x60; (and any bidding field), or the request returns 400. - Google Ads with &#x60;campaignType: \&quot;demand_gen\&quot;&#x60;: the campaign must be Demand Gen (otherwise 400). The new ad group (with its geo, languages, channels and audience from the request) and its ad are created in one atomic request, the ad group PAUSED. Schedule and &#x60;locationTargetingType&#x60; belong to the campaign and return 400. - Google Ads, campaign migrated from Discovery that still targets locations and languages on the campaign: geo and language fields return 400 on a new ad group, which follows the campaign&#39;s targeting. - Google Ads failure: only the entities we authored are cleaned up. The pre-existing parent is left untouched and is never (re)activated. - Reddit Ads: creates a new ad group and the ad under this campaign. &#x60;goal&#x60; may be omitted (the campaign&#39;s objective decides it); any other goal returns 400 naming the one to send. If the ad fails, the new ad group is archived. - Reddit Ads dates: the ad group must start no earlier than a future campaign start and end no later than the campaign end (400 otherwise). Without &#x60;endDate&#x60; it ends with the campaign. - Reddit Ads, campaign without a campaign budget: send &#x60;budgetAmount&#x60;/&#x60;budgetType&#x60; for the new ad group (400 without them). Bid, conversion event and pixel work as on a new campaign. - Reddit Ads under campaign budget optimization: the ad group takes the campaign&#39;s bid, goal type, optimization event and pixel and has no budget of its own. &#x60;budgetAmount&#x60;/&#x60;budgetType&#x60;, bid fields, or another conversion event or pixel return 400, as does an &#x60;endDate&#x60; when the campaign has no end date. - Reddit Ads errors: a campaign of another ad account returns 404, a Reddit Max campaign 422. 
