        /// <summary>
        /// Meta only. Multi-language ads (Dynamic Language Optimization, the \&quot;Languages\&quot; toggle in Ads Manager): ONE ad with per-locale copy and, optionally, per-locale media. Social proof (likes/comments/shares) stays on a SINGLE post instead of splitting across one ad per language.  The ad&#39;s top-level copy is the DEFAULT for every locale you do NOT list, and counts as one of the language variants.  **Text does NOT inherit** (the opposite of what you might expect). Every entry needs its own &#x60;headline&#x60;, &#x60;body&#x60; AND &#x60;description&#x60;, all DISTINCT from each other and from the top-level copy. &#x60;description&#x60; is therefore effectively required on the ad whenever &#x60;translations&#x60; is present, though optional otherwise.  Why: Meta deduplicates identical strings in the asset feed, so two locales sharing a string collapse into one asset.  The create then fails with a misleading \&quot;Too few ... texts provided in asset creation\&quot; (subcode 1885817) naming a field that is present. We validate first and return a 400 naming the locale and field.  Do NOT list &#x60;defaultLocale&#x60; inside &#x60;translations&#x60;: Meta rejects the duplicate with \&quot;The language asset feed includes an unsupported targeting field\&quot; (subcode 1885985).  **Media DOES inherit** and is uploaded once when shared. &#x60;linkUrl&#x60; inherits too: each locale may name its own landing page, and unlisted locales fall back to the top-level &#x60;linkUrl&#x60;.  Meta enforces Dynamic Creative image dimensions on language feeds, so an &#x60;imageUrl&#x60; that works on a normal ad may fail with \&quot;The following images have invalid dimensions for Dynamic Creative\&quot; (subcode 1885558). Video is not affected.  Mutually exclusive with &#x60;dynamicCreative&#x60;, &#x60;placementAssets&#x60;, &#x60;carouselCards&#x60;, &#x60;existingCreativeId&#x60; and &#x60;creatives[]&#x60;: Meta allows one &#x60;asset_feed_spec&#x60; shape per creative. 
